Isis is now claiming responsibility for  a deadly weekend attack on a nightclub  in Turkey surveillance video shows the  suspect opening fire about an hour into  the New Year he has seen approaching the  Istanbul Club with a rifle  the gunman escaped after the attack  victims came from more than a dozen  countries around the world the gunman  killed 39 people many of them from  outside Turkey nearly 70 others were  injured including one American Turkish  media now reports that police have  detained eight suspects who may be  connected to the shooting Jonathan  Vigliotti is in Istanbul outside of the  scene of the attack Jonathan good  morning good morning club Rana is one of  the most popular nightclubs in this city  it's one of those places where people  line up for hours only to be turned away  at the door today a much different scene  police are lined up a blue tarp has been  set up and behind it investigators  working around the clock to collect  evidence from this massive crime scene  [Music]  cell phone video from inside Club Rana  showed a crowd of 600 ringing in the new  year but just one hour into 2017 the  gunman struck surveillance video shows  him exchanging fire with police outside  on the street bullets ricocheting off a  car a camera then captures him shooting  his way into the club killing a police  officer and a civilian inside he  reportedly shot anyone in his path some  club goers initially thought the shots  were fireworks until people started  dropping to the ground the fashionable  Club attracts local celebrities and  tourists from all over the world  Jacob Rocca business owner from  Greenville Delaware was injured in the  attack a bullet reportedly bounced off  his phone and hit him in his leg Rock  spoke this morning about the attack as  he was getting ready to fly to the US  all I can say is it's a massive tragedy  for me I wake up in the unite United  States side breakfast you guys wake up  and have to think of this it's so so sad  and  I really wish everybody here the best  17,000 police were patrolling the  streets on New Year's Eve a middle wave  of attacks in Turkey in 2016 from Isis  and Kurdish separatists fabrina  increased its own security the Interior  Minister believes the man acted alone  and came prepared leaving in his wake a  shattered nightclub and bloody start to  a new year the attacker remains at large  a manhunt for him continues glad the  Interior Minister believes the shooter  changed outfits before disappearing  amidst the chaos Jonathan Vigliotti  reporting from Istanbul thanks Jonathan
 

